-- REJECTED (§8.1). `catIdent` is not injective: `foo bar` and fooBar both
-- mangle to `foo_bar`. Emitting them as nested `let`s makes the inner one
-- shadow the outer, so `a` and `b` would read the same value — 200 in Catala
-- against 101 in L4. Catala's `let` shadows silently, so nothing downstream
-- would have caught it.

@export
GIVETH A NUMBER
total MEANS a PLUS b
  WHERE
    `foo bar` MEANS 1
    fooBar    MEANS 100
    a         MEANS `foo bar`
    b         MEANS fooBar

#EVAL total   -- 101 in L4
